The reacting front of benchmarks/front, the demo's reference in Mercury, on
small grids, so that it keeps building and giving the right cells:
sequentially, and on the host's threads, where OpenMP runs its target
regions when there is no device, each at -O0 and -O2. The values are from
an independent program in Python, which adds and multiplies in the same
order, so every build that does not fuse them gives the same bits.

RUN: merkc -O0 -fdo-loops %S/../../benchmarks/front/front.m -o %t.sequential0
RUN: env FRONT_SIZE=256 FRONT_STEPS=100 %t.sequential0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SQUARE
RUN: env FRONT_SIZE=101 FRONT_STEPS=150 FRONT_SUBSTEPS=20 %t.sequential0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops %S/../../benchmarks/front/front.m -o %t.sequential2
RUN: env FRONT_SIZE=256 FRONT_STEPS=100 %t.sequential2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SQUARE
RUN: env FRONT_SIZE=101 FRONT_STEPS=150 FRONT_SUBSTEPS=20 %t.sequential2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
RUN: merkc -O0 -fopenmp -fdo-loops %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/front/front.m -o %t.host0
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 FRONT_SIZE=101 FRONT_STEPS=150 FRONT_SUBSTEPS=20 %t.host0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/front/front.m -o %t.host2
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 FRONT_SIZE=256 FRONT_STEPS=100 %t.host2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SQUARE
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 FRONT_SIZE=101 FRONT_STEPS=150 FRONT_SUBSTEPS=20 %t.host2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
REQUIRES: libomp

SQUARE: Reacting front, Mercury
SQUARE-NEXT: Grid: 256 x 256 cells
